<section class="page" id="about-page">
  <div class="page-head"><h1>Concepts</h1><p>Eight ideas, each with something to click.</p></div>
  <div class="tabs" id="about-tabs">
    <div class="tabbar scroll" role="tablist">
      <button role="tab" data-tab="org" aria-selected="true">CPU organization</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="cycle" aria-selected="false">Instruction cycle</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="pipe" aria-selected="false">Pipelining</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="cache" aria-selected="false">Cache</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="haz" aria-selected="false">Hazards</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="cpi" aria-selected="false">CPI</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="mips" aria-selected="false">MIPS</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="amd" aria-selected="false">Amdahl's Law</button>
    </div>
    <div class="tabpanel" data-panel="org"><div class="panel concept"><h2>What is CPU organization?</h2><p>How a processor's parts are arranged and connected: control unit, ALU, registers, caches and memory, and the buses between them. Click a block.</p><div class="viz-scroll"><svg id="org-svg"></svg></div><p class="detail-line" id="org-detail">Select a block.</p></div></div>
    <div class="tabpanel" data-panel="cycle" hidden><div class="panel concept"><h2>What is an instruction cycle?</h2><p>The repeating routine a CPU runs for every instruction.</p><div class="cycle-row" id="cyc-row"></div><p class="detail-line" id="cyc-detail">Press play or click a stage.</p><button class="btn primary" id="cyc-play">&#9654; Play cycle</button></div></div>
    <div class="tabpanel" data-panel="pipe" hidden><div class="panel concept"><h2>What is pipelining?</h2><p>Overlapping the stages of different instructions so a new one finishes almost every cycle.</p><div class="seg" id="pp-seg"><button data-pp="seq" aria-pressed="true">Sequential</button><button data-pp="pipe" aria-pressed="false">Pipelined</button></div><label class="stack">Instructions: <b id="pp-n-v">5</b><input type="range" id="pp-n" min="2" max="8" value="5"></label><div id="pp-grid" class="tl-wrap"></div><p class="detail-line" id="pp-detail"></p></div></div>
    <div class="tabpanel" data-panel="cache" hidden><div class="panel concept"><h2>What is cache?</h2><p>A small, fast memory close to the CPU that keeps recently used data. Click addresses to send requests to a real 4-line direct-mapped cache (block size 2).</p><div id="cc-btns" class="btn-row wrap"></div><div id="cc-lines" class="cc-lines"></div><p class="detail-line" id="cc-detail"></p></div></div>
    <div class="tabpanel" data-panel="haz" hidden><div class="panel concept"><h2>What are pipeline hazards?</h2><p>Situations that stop the next instruction from executing in its clock cycle. Pick a type.</p><div class="seg" id="hz-seg"><button data-hz="data" aria-pressed="true">Data</button><button data-hz="control" aria-pressed="false">Control</button><button data-hz="struct" aria-pressed="false">Structural</button></div><div id="hz-grid" class="tl-wrap"></div><p class="detail-line" id="hz-detail"></p></div></div>
    <div class="tabpanel" data-panel="cpi" hidden><div class="panel concept"><h2>What is CPI?</h2><p>Clocks per instruction: the average number of clock cycles each instruction needs. <code>CPI = total cycles / instruction count</code></p><label class="stack">Instruction count <b id="cp-ic-v"></b><input type="range" id="cp-ic" min="10" max="1000" value="100"></label><label class="stack">Total cycles <b id="cp-cy-v"></b><input type="range" id="cp-cy" min="10" max="5000" value="250"></label><div class="big-num"><small>CPI</small><b id="cp-out"></b></div><div class="bars" id="cp-bar"></div></div></div>
    <div class="tabpanel" data-panel="mips" hidden><div class="panel concept"><h2>What is MIPS?</h2><p>Millions of instructions per second. <code>MIPS = IC / (execution time x 10^6) = clock MHz / CPI</code></p><label class="stack">Clock (MHz) <b id="mp-f-v"></b><input type="range" id="mp-f" min="10" max="4000" step="10" value="500"></label><label class="stack">CPI <b id="mp-c-v"></b><input type="range" id="mp-c" min="1" max="8" step="0.1" value="2"></label><div class="big-num"><small>MIPS</small><b id="mp-out"></b></div><div class="bars" id="mp-bar"></div></div></div>
    <div class="tabpanel" data-panel="amd" hidden><div class="panel concept"><h2>What is Amdahl's Law?</h2><p>Speeding up part of a program limits overall gain by the part you did not improve. <code>Speedup = 1 / ((1 - f) + f / s)</code></p><label class="stack">Fraction improved <b id="ad-f-v"></b><input type="range" id="ad-f" min="0" max="0.99" step="0.01" value="0.6"></label><label class="stack">Speedup of that fraction <b id="ad-s-v"></b><input type="range" id="ad-s" min="1" max="64" value="10"></label><div class="big-num"><small>Overall speedup</small><b id="ad-out"></b><span id="ad-lim"></span></div><div class="amd-split" id="ad-split"></div><p class="hint">Full interactive graph: <a href="/performance">Performance Analyzer</a>.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
